From 577ee93fc0af1858a5b84ff8ce5b016a617796f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:45:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] doc,contrib: P2P WebSocket guide with tested privacy recipes

doc/p2p-websocket.md documents serving and dialing P2P over WebSocket,
URL syntax (paths, ?token=, #spki= pins), discovery, compression, and a
privacy and censorship section: threat model, what is and is not
protected, the remaining TLS fingerprint differences, and a legal-risk
note. Its recipes (a node that does not reveal itself, a private-bridge
client, a bridge server with fallback site, a public node behind a TLS
proxy) are exercised end to end by feature_p2p_privacy_recipes.py, with
a forwarding SOCKS5 proxy standing in for Xray or Tor (moved into
test_framework for reuse).

contrib/censorship/ has Xray VLESS+REALITY client/server and Tor bridge
examples providing the -proxy those recipes use.
